{
  "technique": "mutual_information",
  "method": "Continuous k-nearest-neighbor mutual information against capacity, computed separately for each battery and feature with k=3,5,10; Spearman uses the same finite observed pairs, without imputation.",
  "caveats": [
    "MI is measured in nats, is not bounded by 1, has no sign or direction, and does not establish causation.",
    "This finite-sample estimator clips negative estimates to zero. An estimated zero does not prove independence.",
    "All features are treated as continuous. Repeated values, especially reused EIS measurements, challenge that assumption. Scikit-learn adds small seeded noise to break ties; ties are counted in records. This numerical handling neither creates new measurements nor fixes the dependence between cycles sharing the same measurement.",
    "Neighbor settings change the bias/variance tradeoff. The three estimates are sensitivity checks, not confidence bounds.",
    "Cycles are ordered, serially dependent observations. Shared aging trends can raise MI and correlation. No raw-row permutation p-values or claims of independent predictive value are made.",
    "Only valid finite feature\u2013capacity pairs are used for each feature. Flagged charge values remain missing; no values are imputed.",
    "Nearest EIS alignment may select future measurements, and EIS completion times are unknown. Re/Rct associations do not certify availability at an earlier prediction moment.",
    "delta_T_max needs the full discharge; delta_V_ohmic needs the load step after discharge starts. rest_time_hours includes intervening charging and is not pure idle rest.",
    "All four batteries are exploratory, with no held-out cells or predictive model. Observed associations are not a universal ranking."
  ],
